Cuts of the FLAC decoder testbench for nx.io's FLAC tests

The files ietf_*.flac are cut from the FLAC decoder testbench by Martijn
van Beurden, the IETF CELLAR working group's FLAC test files:
https://github.com/ietf-wg-cellar/flac-test-files, commit
aa7b0c6cf32994c106ae517a08134c28a96ff5b2. Its LICENSE.txt states:

  To the extent possible under law, the person who associated CC0 with
  FLAC decoder testbench has waived all copyright and related or
  neighboring rights to FLAC decoder testbench.

ietf_<set>_<nn>.flac is the file of that number in subset/, uncommon/ or
faulty/, modified: a valid file keeps its first frames unchanged, its
STREAMINFO states their length, frame sizes and MD5, as FFmpeg decodes
them, and its seek points within them stay; other metadata blocks are
dropped, but for a Vorbis comment of at most 4 KiB. A file the decoder
must refuse keeps its metadata and first frames, or its first 4 KiB, but
for padding. ietf.tsv states each valid cut's facts and the MD5 of
FFmpeg's samples.
